# Normalise line endings.
#
# Everything in this repo is text, and it is edited from Windows, Linux and
# whatever CI runs on. Without this, Git stores whatever each machine happens to
# write: a file saved with CRLF then shows as entirely rewritten the next time
# someone on another platform touches it, and a one-line change arrives as a
# 400-line diff nobody can review.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores LF in the repository and leaves working copies to
# each platform's own convention, which is what the "LF will be replaced by
# CRLF" notice on Windows is describing. That notice is expected and harmless.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so Git must not touch the bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
